title: Dr. Ben Barr joins Seo Lab as a new postdoctoral researcher!
date: 2025-10-13
---

<div style="flex: 2;">
  <p>
    <a href="https://www2.whoi.edu/staff/bbarr/">Dr. Ben Barr</a> is an expert in sea spray modeling and air–sea interaction under high-wind conditions. 
    He has published influential studies on sea spray parameterizations 
    (<a href="https://doi.org/10.1175/JAS-D-22-0126.1">Barr et al., 2023</a>) 
    and their effects on tropical cyclones 
    (<a href="https://doi.org/10.1029/2024MS004550">Barr et al., 2025</a>).
    Before joining UH, Ben was a postdoctoral researcher at the Woods Hole Oceanographic Institution (WHOI) from 2023 to 2025. He earned his Ph.D. in Atmospheric Sciences from the University of Washington in 2023 under the guidance of Prof. Shuyi Chen. At UH, Ben will continue advancing sea spray modeling and investigating surface wave impacts on air–sea fluxes, contributing to the development of a sea-spray–aware next-generation COARE bulk flux algorithm. Ben will work remotely from Austin, Teaxs. Welcome Ben!
  </p>
